{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create","id":1107618,"title":"Trinary Computers, how create?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-25T06:53:44-07:00","id":1107618,"title":"Trinary Computers, how create?","content":"I have a question, how Virtual Adepts (and Technocrats) create Trinary Computers (in-game and game mechanics)?<br /> <br /> I can't find anything about this, Trinary Computers are Wonders or very advanced mundane tech?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T07:09:46-07:00","id":1107625,"title":"","content":"The new Book of Secrets goes into them a little bit where they are listed as Enlightened Hypertech, thus making them equvilant to a technological focus at the very least and full blown wonders otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T11:27:21-07:00","id":1107692,"title":"","content":"I've always treated them at Hypertech tools which in sleeper hands tend to break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:21:46-07:00","id":1107734,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd treat them like the various other 'not quite enlightened' bits of gear the Technocracy uses. It's a mundane piece of equipment with permanent magical effects on it. In Game Terms it'd be a Trinket.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:32:45-07:00","id":1107740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1107692#post1107692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always treated them at Hypertech tools which in sleeper hands tend to break.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Setun\" target=\"_blank\"> Real life examples seemed to have a great deal of durability...</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:54:30-07:00","id":1107750,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Trinary computers, conceptually, are just machines that use three states instead of binary's two. Dur-hey. There's nothing supernatural about it; as shown, they've been made before. The structure isn't used in regular computing more out of everyone adopting binary and building the entire field of computer science around it. The use of three state programming is totally possible, and likely employed by certain dedicated hobbyists. And the Internet has no shortage of dedicated hobbyists, so a Sleeper versed in computers would see a Trinary Computer and think it's weird but not impossible.<br /> <br /> And if we don't have a computer literate sleeper around, checking its internal processes, we wouldn't have any way of knowing if the laptop sitting on the table was Trinary at all, or merely a powerful binary system. In and of itself, a Trinary Computer would not, logically, be Paradoxical, although some of the tasks it can be made to do (or, in the case of a Trinary computer that is also a Wonder, what features it comes built-in with) might be Vulgar. Just having it isn't necessarily going to rustle Reality's jimmies. An unAwakened person with a dot or two in Hypertech would be able to use it the same way a person might employ their Computer ability to use a regular computer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T20:01:33-07:00","id":1108242,"title":"","content":"As others have said, ternary computers <i>are</i> a thing. At most, they'd be a focus/tool.<br /> <br /> Now, if you imbued them with <i>permanent </i>autonomic functions, and/or varying degrees of artificial intelligence up to and including sapience, as many mages with computing-related paradigms are wont to do, they'd become a Device/Wonder with all the benefits, drawbacks, and requirements to create that entails. Temporarily, that can be done entirely within the purview of Effects.<br /> <br /> ...and I'll be damned if that didn't give me one hell of an idea for a story. VA imparts his computer with sentience, dies or falls into Quiet, and the sentient computer is now dying of &quot;old age&quot; (i.e. the Effect is nearing its end). So many ethical quandaries and dilemmas for a group of players to muck through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T00:14:32-07:00","id":1108649,"title":"","content":"The rules for trinary computers were last seen in the second edition corebook. The other posters here are completely wrong, because the idea behind VA trinary computers is closer to that of quantum computers than just having three states.<br /> Mechanically trinary computers allow VAs to pre-cast a few spells and unleash them at a later time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T16:47:35-07:00","id":1419480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1108649#post1108649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for trinary computers were last seen in the second edition corebook. The other posters here are completely wrong, because the idea behind VA trinary computers is closer to that of quantum computers than just having three states.<br /> Mechanically trinary computers allow VAs to pre-cast a few spells and unleash them at a later time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I read in an M20 sourcebook that the technical term for in-universe state-of-the-art trinary computers would be &quot;quinary computers,&quot; by which I presume they mean a computer that runs on qutrits, the trinary equivalent of qubits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26432,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","user":"JagneStormskull","date":". 10-23-2020, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T02:40:45-07:00","id":1420093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1419480#post1419480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I read in an M20 sourcebook that the technical term for in-universe state-of-the-art trinary computers would be &amp;quot;quinary computers,&amp;quot; by which I presume they mean a computer that runs on qutrits, the trinary equivalent of qubits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what any of that means explain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T07:50:18-07:00","id":1420123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1108649#post1108649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for trinary computers were last seen in the second edition corebook. The other posters here are completely wrong, because the idea behind VA trinary computers is closer to that of quantum computers than just having three states.<br /> Mechanically trinary computers allow VAs to pre-cast a few spells and unleash them at a later time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quantum is way better. Each circuit can generate a range of numbers between 0 and 1, expresses as a decimal. It is based on the probability of a particle being present. I could see trinary computers being used in a specific way in Mage. If you were looking at a part of the Digital Web and wanted to measure the associations of things with the Wyrm, Weaver and Wild, trinary computers could neatly organize that data. Any part of the Tellurian could be scanned this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T18:50:46-07:00","id":1420378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420093#post1420093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no idea what any of that means explain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a bit, the basic unit of binary logic, is how a regular, digital computer processes data. 0/1; Off/On; how the Mage books use the term, No/Yes.<br /> <br /> Now, brace yourself, because I might sound a bit Etherite/VA here, but this is real computer science.<br /> <br /> A quantum bit, or <b>qubit</b>, the basic unit of quantum computing, takes advantage of the Heisenberg Uncertainty Principle in order to process data in an infinite superposition of states between 0 and 1 until observed. Think of it like Schrodinger's Cat; you don't know what state the cat is in until you open the box; it's the same thing with a qubit. Because of this, a string of <i>n</i> qubits can hold much more information that a string of <i>n</i> classical bits.<br /> <br /> A trit, the basic unit of ternary logic, is how a trinary computer processes data. 1/2/0; True/False/Unknown. Now, a quantum trit, or <b>qutrit</b>, the basic unit of quantum trinary computing, or <b>quinary computing</b>, as M20 calls it, exists in a superposition of these three states; because of that, a string of <i>n</i> 3-Dimensional qutrits can hold much more than a string of <i>n</i> 2-Dimensional qubits. If someone could make a quinary computer portable (which, since there are VAs who have state-of-the-art trinary smart phones in M20, so they presumably have), it would most likely be the limit of what humanity could accomplish in terms of portable or personal computing power.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20080229001836/http://www.physorg.com/news123244300.html\" target=\"_blank\">N</a>ote: a computer scientist that I have access to says that the following article's show of the level of data that each of those can contain is inaccurate. However, it's still a good primer on the subject of qutrits beyond what I have given here.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20080229001836/http://www.physorg.com/news123244300.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20080229...123244300.html </a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26432,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","user":"JagneStormskull","date":". 10-26-2020, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T23:23:17-07:00","id":1420409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420378#post1420378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a bit, the basic unit of binary logic, is how a regular, digital computer processes data. 0/1; Off/On; how the Mage books use the term, No/Yes.<br /> <br /> Now, brace yourself, because I might sound a bit Etherite/VA here, but this is real computer science.<br /> <br /> A quantum bit, or <b>qubit</b>, the basic unit of quantum computing, takes advantage of the Heisenberg Uncertainty Principle in order to process data in an infinite superposition of states between 0 and 1 until observed. Think of it like Schrodinger's Cat; you don't know what state the cat is in until you open the box; it's the same thing with a qubit. Because of this, a string of <i>n</i> qubits can hold much more information that a string of <i>n</i> classical bits.<br /> <br /> A trit, the basic unit of ternary logic, is how a trinary computer processes data. 1/2/0; True/False/Unknown. Now, a quantum trit, or <b>qutrit</b>, the basic unit of quantum trinary computing, or <b>quinary computing</b>, as M20 calls it, exists in a superposition of these three states; because of that, a string of <i>n</i> 3-Dimensional qutrits can hold much more than a string of <i>n</i> 2-Dimensional qubits. If someone could make a quinary computer portable (which, since there are VAs who have state-of-the-art trinary smart phones in M20, so they presumably have), it would most likely be the limit of what humanity could accomplish in terms of portable or personal computing power.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20080229001836/http://www.physorg.com/news123244300.html\" target=\"_blank\">N</a>ote: a computer scientist that I have access to says that the following article's show of the level of data that each of those can contain is inaccurate. However, it's still a good primer on the subject of qutrits beyond what I have given here.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20080229001836/http://www.physorg.com/news123244300.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20080229...123244300.html </a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We are humbled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T05:23:03-07:00","id":1420433,"title":"","content":"What VAs call \u201cTrinary\u201d and what real-world computer scientists call \u201ctrinary\u201d are two different things. (I'll capitalize Trinary when referring to the former.) In VA terms, \u201cTrinary\u201d isn't merely having three states instead of two; it's about being able to express and process concepts that binary simply can't handle. More generally, the VA notion isn't so much about binary or trinary at all, so much as it's about Turing Machines and going beyond them. Real-world computers can be really powerful; but conceptually, they're at best Turing-equivalent and in practice \u201cTuring-inferior\u201d. VA-style Trinary computers are capable of operations that a Turing Machine is incapable of. <br /> <br /> While the existing Mage books invariably phrase this in terms of adding \u201cmaybe\u201d to the \u201cyes\u201d and \u201cno\u201d options, that can't be technically accurate, as a three-state machine can easily be modeled by a two-state machine. Conversely, VA-style Trinary computers are also stated to be able to \u201cmodel human thought\u201d, which \u2014 in the setting of Mage, at least \u2014 is something that a Turing Machine is incapable of. As such, the use of the term \u201cTrinary\u201d by the VAs is more allegorical than literal: it's \u201ca step up\u201d from normal computing, capable of processing things in ways that are impossible even in theory for regular computers. <br /> <br /> An Etherite might phrase this in terms of quantum computing; they are, after all, the faction responsible for introducing Quantum Mechanics into the Consensus. And arguably, that's how they tend to see the Correspondence Sphere: the bonds of Sympathy are Quantum Entanglements; Co-Location is a superposition of states; and so on. <br /> <br /> But that's not how the VAs think; for all of its descriptive power, Quantum Mechanics is still fundamentally part of the natural sciences: physics, chemistry, biology, etc. VAs are more about the formal sciences: logic, mathematics, statistics, information theory, and so on. They're not going to talk or think I'm terms of qubits or qutrits; as powerful as those notions are, even <i>they</i> don't really capture the processing capability of what the VAs call a Trinary computer. <br /> <br /> And that's why Trinary computers are Wonders: they interact with reality in ways that are to regular computers as the Awakened are to Sleepers. <br /> <br /> And for what it's worth, that's also what differentiates the Digital Web from the Internet: the Internet is Binary in VA lingo, while the Digital Web is Trinary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T17:20:55-07:00","id":1420592,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420433#post1420433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What VAs call \u201cTrinary\u201d and what real-world computer scientists call \u201ctrinary\u201d are two different things. (I'll capitalize Trinary when referring to the former.) In VA terms, \u201cTrinary\u201d isn't merely having three states instead of two; it's about being able to express and process concepts that binary simply can't handle. More generally, the VA notion isn't so much about binary or trinary at all, so much as it's about Turing Machines and going beyond them. Real-world computers can be really powerful; but conceptually, they're at best Turing-equivalent and in practice \u201cTuring-inferior\u201d. VA-style Trinary computers are capable of operations that a Turing Machine is incapable of.<br /> <br /> While the existing Mage books invariably phrase this in terms of adding \u201cmaybe\u201d to the \u201cyes\u201d and \u201cno\u201d options, that can't be technically accurate, as a three-state machine can easily be modeled by a two-state machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>2*3=6<br /> The first three prime numbers multiply out to 30 (2*3*5).<br /> The number thirty is the center of a cool discovery in math, which you might already know about. The Prime Echo (not the Prime Spiral, a different discovery that is harder to explain). On a number line, pairs of primes are found at equal distance from thirty. They drew circles connecting the prime pairs and it looks like a ripple in water. Apparently, there is a relationship between theoretical numbers on the circles that don't fit on the real-number-line.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420433#post1420433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, VA-style Trinary computers are also stated to be able to \u201cmodel human thought\u201d, which \u2014 in the setting of Mage, at least \u2014 is something that a Turing Machine is incapable of.</div> </div> </div> </div>This leads me to an aspect of the game that, I feel, needs further development - Badly. The Pattern Spheres, Prime, Matter, Life, Forces, are explained in better detail, in relation to each other. A certain amount of flowing quintessence fuels an individual pattern. A living tree, a pile of wood and a roaring fire can be seen as conversions of raw substance into another form.<br /> <br /> The Mind is described as a Pattern. Can a Nephandi extract quintessence from a target by rending his psyche, leaving his life pattern intact? If so, how much? Mages can steal a Changeling's Dreaming location by extracting it for quint. When it comes to a human mind, how can it be quantified, rules wise? Wellsprings produce quint from people getting excited about something.<br /> <br /> If the mind is a Pattern and everyone has an Avatar, these are two different Patterns. So, you can't convert a psyche into a Spirit the way a broken tree branch converts from a Life Pattern to a Matter Pattern. The person with the psyche already has an Avatar/Spirit.<br /> <br /> One could look at from the perspective of aging. Children see the world with great fascination. They are recently incarnated. Their Spirit/Avatar is more active, but their Mind has only accrued a fraction of the data that it will have at the end of life. The old man with more accumulated knowledge has lost that sense of wonder. His Avatar wants to return to the Umbra to be renewed. I'm thinking from a Euthanatos perspective, as well.<br /> <br /> Returning to the subject of computers, if a model of human thought can exist as Trinary Data, is it a Forces Pattern? In the brain, memories are stored as pathways linking neurons all over the brain. Can we assign a value in gigabytes or volts to a dream and have a corresponding value in Quintessence?<br /> <br /> Is a resource other than Quintessence needed as a measure of the Mind Pattern?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420433#post1420433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's why Trinary computers are Wonders: they interact with reality in ways that are to regular computers as the Awakened are to Sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you could bring a Sleeper to a Sanctum and link his brain to a VA/SoE Trinary computer, he would awaken?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420433#post1420433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for what it's worth, that's also what differentiates the Digital Web from the Internet: the Internet is Binary in VA lingo, while the Digital Web is Trinary.</div> </div> </div> </div>A sleeper's un-awakened avatar exists in the Umbra, while his Mind rests on the Life/Forces Pattern of his brain. The Digital Web is part of the Umbra. A brain-machine circuit connected to a Trinary computer connects all of these things. Maybe it's too much and he becomes a Marauder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":".  their/there 10-28-2020, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T20:35:46-07:00","id":1420606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420592#post1420592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> 2*3=6<br /> The first three prime numbers multiply out to 30 (2*3*5).<br /> The number thirty is the center of a cool discovery in math, which you might already know about. The Prime Echo (not the Prime Spiral, a different discovery that is harder to explain). On a number line, pairs of primes are found at equal distance from thirty. They drew circles connecting the prime pairs and it looks like a ripple in water. Apparently, their is a relationship between theoretical numbers on the circles that don't fit on the real-number-line.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to look into the complex-number plane. There's a lot of fascinating stuff there, such as the Gaussian Integers (which include the Gaussian Primes, which do indeed have a circular pattern to them) to the Mandelbrot Set (which is a fundamental set, not merely an artifact of one particular way of representing the complex numbers). <br /> <br /> And even that merely scratches the surface. What I was trying to say had more to do with Godel's Incompleteness Theorem in mathematics (there are always going to be true statements in an axiomatic system that can't be proven by the axioms), and the Halting Problem in information science (there are programs that will never halt and that no other program can predict will never halt): both place limits on what their respective subjects can do through the usual means, and both point to the existence of something that transcends the usual means. In particular, the human mind is capable of things that a computer isn't. <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420592#post1420592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThis leads me to an aspect of the game that, I feel, needs further development - Badly. The Pattern Spheres, Prime, Matter, Life, Forces, are explained in better detail, in relation to each other. A certain amount of flowing quintessence fuels an individual pattern. A living tree, a pile of wood and a roaring fire can be seen as conversions of raw substance into another form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick: Prime isn't a Pattern Sphere. Thinking of it as such causes you to miss possibilities such at the Syndicate's Primal Utility, which doesn't map well to the notion that Prime deals with something that's energy-like. (Although, see below.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420592#post1420592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe Mind is described as a Pattern. Can a Nephandi extract quintessence from a target by rending his psyche, leaving his life pattern intact? If so, how much? Mages can steal a Changeling's Dreaming location by extracting it for quint. When it comes to a human mind, how can it be quantified, rules wise? Wellsprings produce quint from people getting excited about something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind isn't a Pattern Sphere, either; the only Pattern Spheres are Forces, Life, and Matter. What they have in common is that they deal with aspects of physical reality. <br /> <br /> Now, you <i>can</i> think of Mind and Prime as dealing with Patterns, too \u2014 but only if you go with a broader, and thus less defined, notion of \u201cPattern\u201d. In particular, this broader notion of \u201cPattern\u201d doesn't include the ability to destroy a Pattern in order to extract Quintessence from it; that's something that's specific to the kind of Patterns that Forces, Life, and Matter represent. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420592#post1420592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIf the mind is a Pattern and everyone has an Avatar, these are two different Patterns. So, you can't convert a psyche into a Spirit the way a broken tree branch converts from a Life Pattern to a Matter Pattern. The person with the psyche already has an Avatar/Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Avatars aren't governed by Spirit; in fact, there is no longer Sphere that deals with the Avatar. In general, it tends to require conjunctional use of several Spheres to deal with the Avatar. Spirit is frequently one of them; but then, so is Prime. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420592#post1420592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOne could look at from the perspective of aging. Children see the world with great fascination. They are recently incarnated. Their Spirit/Avatar is more active, but their Mind has only accrued a fraction of the data that it will have at the end of life.</div> </div> </div> </div> Mind and Data are two different things, too. I tend to view them relating to each other in a manner similar to how Life and Matter relate to each other. I also sometimes think of Prime as relating to the two of them in a manner similar to how Forces relates to Life and Matter; but it's not an exact match. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420592#post1420592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Returning to the subject of computers, if a model of human thought can exist as Trinary Data, is it a Forces Pattern? In the brain, memories are stored as pathways linking neurons all over the brain. Can we assign a value in gigabytes or volts to a dream and have a corresponding value in Quintessence?</div> </div> </div> </div>The notion that memories are stored as pathways linking neutrons all over the brain is a very Enlightened Science concept; and in the world of Mage, it may not actually be true: the only evidence we have that it <i>is</i> true comes from\u2026 Instruments of Enlightened Science. <br /> <br /> Data isn't a Forces Pattern; it's a Correspondence Pattern. In particular, there's a reason why the NWO's version of Correspondence is called Data: to the NWO (and also to the VAs, who pioneered the Data variant before largely abandoning it), Correspondence is the Sphere that governs mathematics, information science, statistics, etc. \u2014 in short, the apartment formal sciences. It deals with spatial relationships, too; but that's because geometry is a branch of mathematics. <br /> <br /> Though again, I refer you to my earlier remarks about broader and narrower definitions of \u201cPattern\u201d. In this case, I'm referring to the broader definition. Incidentally, there's a whole philosophy of science that says that the Pattern Spheres are fundamental, and all other Patterns are emergent properties of those three. It's called materialism. And while it's not listed among the Paradigms thus far published in M20 and its supplements, it very much <i>is</i> a Paradigm. Maybe phrase it as \u201cEverything is Physical\u201d. You were expressing this Paradigm earlier when you talked about patterns of energy in the brain's neurons. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420592#post1420592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you could bring a Sleeper to a Sanctum and link his brain to a VA/SoE Trinary computer, he would awaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420592#post1420592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sleeper's un-awakened avatar exists in the Umbra, while his Mind rests on the Life/Forces Pattern of his brain. The Digital Web is part of the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>No on all counts. The Avatar does not exist in the Umbra. It can <i>manifest</i> there; but it can also manifest in the mage's mind or in the physical world; or even in other ways. The Materialistic Paradigm describes the Mind residing in the Life/Forces Pattern of the brain; but less materialistic Paradigms tend to view the Mind as something distinct from the body, though able to influence and be influenced by it. <br /> <br /> And the Digital Web isn't in the Umbra. It <i>intersects with</i> the Umbra, but is its own thing. More generally, the VA cosmological model (as presented in the Revised VA Tradition Book) is that of the Hypersphere: a higher-dimensional model of reality where the center is the Correspondence Point, the skin of the Hypersphere is what the other Traditions view as the Tellurian (the physical world, the Umbrae, the Dreaming, and so on), and the \u201cspace between\u201d the Tellurian and the Correspondence Point is the Digital Web (both the explored and the as-yet undiscovered sectors).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T14:38:06-07:00","id":1420716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420433#post1420433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What VAs call \u201cTrinary\u201d and what real-world computer scientists call \u201ctrinary\u201d are two different things. (I'll capitalize Trinary when referring to the former.) In VA terms, \u201cTrinary\u201d isn't merely having three states instead of two; it's about being able to express and process concepts that binary simply can't handle. More generally, the VA notion isn't so much about binary or trinary at all, so much as it's about Turing Machines and going beyond them. Real-world computers can be really powerful; but conceptually, they're at best Turing-equivalent and in practice \u201cTuring-inferior\u201d. VA-style Trinary computers are capable of operations that a Turing Machine is incapable of.<br /> <br /> While the existing Mage books invariably phrase this in terms of adding \u201cmaybe\u201d to the \u201cyes\u201d and \u201cno\u201d options, that can't be technically accurate, as a three-state machine can easily be modeled by a two-state machine. Conversely, VA-style Trinary computers are also stated to be able to \u201cmodel human thought\u201d, which \u2014 in the setting of Mage, at least \u2014 is something that a Turing Machine is incapable of. As such, the use of the term \u201cTrinary\u201d by the VAs is more allegorical than literal: it's \u201ca step up\u201d from normal computing, capable of processing things in ways that are impossible even in theory for regular computers.<br /> <br /> An Etherite might phrase this in terms of quantum computing; they are, after all, the faction responsible for introducing Quantum Mechanics into the Consensus. And arguably, that's how they tend to see the Correspondence Sphere: the bonds of Sympathy are Quantum Entanglements; Co-Location is a superposition of states; and so on.<br /> <br /> But that's not how the VAs think; for all of its descriptive power, Quantum Mechanics is still fundamentally part of the natural sciences: physics, chemistry, biology, etc. VAs are more about the formal sciences: logic, mathematics, statistics, information theory, and so on. They're not going to talk or think I'm terms of qubits or qutrits; as powerful as those notions are, even <i>they</i> don't really capture the processing capability of what the VAs call a Trinary computer.<br /> <br /> And that's why Trinary computers are Wonders: they interact with reality in ways that are to regular computers as the Awakened are to Sleepers.<br /> <br /> And for what it's worth, that's also what differentiates the Digital Web from the Internet: the Internet is Binary in VA lingo, while the Digital Web is Trinary.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make an interesting point about VAs and the formal sciences, however I would like to note that quantum computation is an intersection of quantum mechanics, computer engineering, and <b>theoretical computer science</b>, the formal science that makes up the foundation of VA... I don't know what you'd call the occult equivalent of theology... arcanology? Let's go with that. Quantum computation has even been incorporated into automata theory, a key part of VA arcanology, with the quantum Turing Machine, quantum pushdown automaton, and other such theories.<br /> <br /> The reason I made the hypothesis that capital-t Trinary computers run on qutrits is that page 122 of M20's Book of Secrets calls the state of the art Trinary computers &quot;<b>Quinary computers</b>,&quot; implying <b>Quantum-trinary</b>.<br /> <br /> I made the theory earlier that a portable quinary computer would be the pinnacle of humanity's technological progress, however, it is also impossible according to what we know about the laws of our world due to the low-energy states required to induce quantum computing. A portable quinary computer would be a Wonder, because of the fact that it would violate the Laws of Thermodynamics by keeping itself that cold for so long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26432,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","user":"JagneStormskull","date":". 10-28-2020, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T18:37:09-07:00","id":1420739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420606#post1420606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might want to look into the complex-number plane. There's a lot of fascinating stuff there, such as the Gaussian Integers (which include the Gaussian Primes, which do indeed have a circular pattern to them) to the Mandelbrot Set (which is a fundamental set, not merely an artifact of one particular way of representing the complex numbers).<br /> <br /> And even that merely scratches the surface. What I was trying to say had more to do with Godel's Incompleteness Theorem in mathematics (there are always going to be true statements in an axiomatic system that can't be proven by the axioms), and the Halting Problem in information science (there are programs that will never halt and that no other program can predict will never halt): both place limits on what their respective subjects can do through the usual means, and both point to the existence of something that transcends the usual means. In particular, the human mind is capable of things that a computer isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be a year before I commit to understanding these theories - even cursorily. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420606#post1420606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick: Prime isn't a Pattern Sphere. Thinking of it as such causes you to miss possibilities such at the Syndicate's Primal Utility, which doesn't map well to the notion that Prime deals with something that's energy-like. (Although, see below.)</div> </div> </div> </div>True. It's not listed in the M20 Core entry alongside the three that are listed. I just think of Prime as so integral to the actual listed Pattern Spheres that I unconsciously classified it as such. A Life Pattern can't exist without quintessence flowing through it and their is finite quintessence in any finite space where existing patterns hold the most. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420606#post1420606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind isn't a Pattern Sphere, either; the only Pattern Spheres are Forces, Life, and Matter. What they have in common is that they deal with aspects of physical reality.<br /> <br /> Now, you <i>can</i> think of Mind and Prime as dealing with Patterns, too \u2014 but only if you go with a broader, and thus less defined, notion of \u201cPattern\u201d. In particular, this broader notion of \u201cPattern\u201d doesn't include the ability to destroy a Pattern in order to extract Quintessence from it; that's something that's specific to the kind of Patterns that Forces, Life, and Matter represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here, I wasn't making the same error. I knew it was not listed as such, because it is not a material pattern. When you edit someone memories with Mind 4, you are altering something that you mean to hold together. It is a Structure of some kind. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420606#post1420606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avatars aren't governed by Spirit; in fact, there is no longer Sphere that deals with the Avatar. In general, it tends to require conjunctional use of several Spheres to deal with the Avatar. Spirit is frequently one of them; but then, so is Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 Core, p522, Spirit 5, &quot;...and bestow the awful sentence of Gilgul - the destruction of a mage' Avatar.&quot;. How Do you Do That has entries about causing Possession and raising the dead, but it seems to be talking about non-mages' avatars. I could not find anything in HDYDT that contradicts the earlier Spirit Sphere Entry. It isn't that I actually want it to be the case for the sake of having been right on at least one thing. I find the idea that a character - NPC even - loses their soul because of another Mage's successful Arete roll or the target failing willpower to be draconian, story and rules wise. Don't get me started on the Nephandi's Caul. Will have to check Gods and Monsters section on avatars to see anything else about this.<br /> <br /> Satyros Brucato said that the original writing for Dreamspeakers was one of his biggest regrets, because they were depicted as only dealing with the Umbra and not being politically active in any way. I always ran Dreamspeakers as people existing in a harsh Earthly reality that mandated them to be actors in politics and media. But even when they were said to be relegated to dealing with the Umbra, that is a huge domain. It is perhaps the only theater of conflict where the Traditions would stand some chance against the Technocracy, given the number of enemies the Void Engineers have made there. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420606#post1420606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind and Data are two different things, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have gotten to this earlier in my reply:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420592#post1420592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bCan we assign a value in gigabytes</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant data like gigs, not Data Sphere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420606#post1420606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Data isn't a Forces Pattern; it's a Correspondence Pattern. In particular, there's a reason why the NWO's version of Correspondence is called Data: to the NWO (and also to the VAs, who pioneered the Data variant before largely abandoning it), Correspondence is the Sphere that governs mathematics, information science, statistics, etc. \u2014 in short, the apartment formal sciences. It deals with spatial relationships, too; but that's because geometry is a branch of mathematics.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some things about the game that I find arbitrary. Besides Mind, Correspondence is one of the most powerful Spheres. Faced with a difficult situation? - Teleport to England (preferably the countryside). A little paradox to escape with your life. Then, adding the ability to alter computer data from a distance, you can shut down a power station from a distance, where a Forces Mage would have to get into line of sight and attack the building's exposed parts. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420606#post1420606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, there's a whole philosophy of science that says that the Pattern Spheres are fundamental, and all other Patterns are emergent properties of those three. It's called materialism. And while it's not listed among the Paradigms thus far published in M20 and its supplements, it very much <i>is</i> a Paradigm. Maybe phrase it as \u201cEverything is Physical\u201d. You were expressing this Paradigm earlier when you talked about patterns of energy in the brain's neurons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do find alternatives to materialism interesting. This interview had me up late. Couldn't stop listening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Az18Onc0e58&amp;ab_channel=metaRising\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Az18Onc0e58&amp;ab_channel=metaRising\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Az18Onc0e58&amp;ab_channel=metaRising\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Az18Onc0e58&amp;ab_channel=metaRising </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420606#post1420606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No on all counts. The Avatar does not exist in the Umbra. It can <i>manifest</i> there; but it can also manifest in the mage's mind or in the physical world; or even in other ways. The Materialistic Paradigm describes the Mind residing in the Life/Forces Pattern of the brain; but less materialistic Paradigms tend to view the Mind as something distinct from the body, though able to influence and be influenced by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose telling new players their character is special for having an avatar, you have to make it this elusive thing that can't be nailed down. I have not yet given Book Of The Fallen a complete read... There, said don't get me started on the Caul and look at me go. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420606#post1420606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Digital Web isn't in the Umbra. It <i>intersects with</i> the Umbra, but is its own thing. More generally, the VA cosmological model (as presented in the Revised VA Tradition Book) is that of the Hypersphere: a higher-dimensional model of reality where the center is the Correspondence Point, the skin of the Hypersphere is what the other Traditions view as the Tellurian (the physical world, the Umbrae, the Dreaming, and so on), and the \u201cspace between\u201d the Tellurian and the Correspondence Point is the Digital Web (both the explored and the as-yet undiscovered sectors).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Is there a TV-land?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T19:49:46-07:00","id":1420752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420739#post1420739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be a year before I commit to understanding these theories - even cursorily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaussian Integers are simple enough, once you've got a handle on complex numbers; they're merely those complex numbers where both the Real and Imaginary components are integers; so they form a two-dimensional grid of dots. Because Complex numbers have a well-defined rule for multiplication, it follows that you can define which other Gaussian Integers a given one is divisible by and which ones it isn't divisible by; and the definition of a Prime can be extended to them simply by saying that a Gaussian Prime is a Gaussian Integer that isn't divisible by anything other than a unit (i.e., 1, -1, i, or-i; literally everything is divisible by all of the units), by itself, or by one of its cohorts (where a cohort is defined by the division resulting in a unit other than 1; so -2 is a cohort of 2 because 2/-2=-1, a unit other than 1). <br /> <br /> And when you map out the Gaussian Primes, you get a roughly circular pattern. <br /> <br /> Godel's Incompleteness Theorem is a bit harder to wrap your head around, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420739#post1420739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. It's not listed in the M20 Core entry alongside the three that are listed. I just think of Prime as so integral to the actual listed Pattern Spheres that I unconsciously classified it as such. A Life Pattern can't exist without quintessence flowing through it and their is finite quintessence in any finite space where existing patterns hold the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime <i>is</i> intimately related to the Pattern Spheres, yes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420739#post1420739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here, I wasn't making the same error. I knew it was not listed as such, because it is not a material pattern. When you edit someone memories with Mind 4, you are altering something that you mean to hold together. It is a Structure of some kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. But the same can be said of <i>every</i> Sphere; that's what I was referring to when I talked about \u201cPattern\u201d being usable in either a narrow way (as it is with the Pattern Spheres) or a broad way (as with the sense in which every Sphere can be said to deal with patterns). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420739#post1420739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 Core, p522, Spirit 5, \u201c...and bestow the awful sentence of Gilgul - the destruction of a mage' Avatar.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I can kill a person using just Life; that doesn't mean that a person is composed solely of a Life Pattern, or that everything the person is resides within his or her Life Pattern. Similarly, the fact that Spirit alone can destroy an Avatar doesn't mean that an Avatar consists of a Spirit pattern alone, or that it wholely resides within a Spirit pattern. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420739#post1420739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How Do you Do That has entries about causing Possession and raising the dead, but it seems to be talking about non-mages' avatars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, because the <i>only</i> thing you lose when Gilgulled is your ability to work Magick: Possession still works normally on you, as does the Afterlife and necromancy. So I don't buy that the human soul and the Avatar are the same thing. I <i>can</i> buy that the Avatar is likely part of the human soul, or at the very least connected to it (much as the Mind <i>might</i> be part of the Life pattern, and if not it's demonstrably connected to it). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420739#post1420739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could not find anything in HDYDT that contradicts the earlier Spirit Sphere Entry. It isn't that I actually want it to be the case for the sake of having been right on at least one thing. I find the idea that a character - NPC even - loses their soul because of another Mage's successful Arete roll or the target failing willpower to be draconian, story and rules wise. Don't get me started on the Nephandi's Caul. Will have to check Gods and Monsters section on avatars to see anything else about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just point of here that is a lot easier to screw something up than it is to affect it <i>without</i> screwing it up. That's why the Cauls make a certain amount of perverse sense to me: inverting an Avatar is basically a way of screwing it up. <br /> <br /> That said, Cauls are generally found, not made; the Nephandi don't actually have Magick that can invert an Avatar. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420739#post1420739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satyros Brucato said that the original writing for Dreamspeakers was one of his biggest regrets, because they were depicted as only dealing with the Umbra and not being politically active in any way. I always ran Dreamspeakers as people existing in a harsh Earthly reality that mandated them to be actors in politics and media. But even when they were said to be relegated to dealing with the Umbra, that is a huge domain. It is perhaps the only theater of conflict where the Traditions would stand some chance against the Technocracy, given the number of enemies the Void Engineers have made there.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true, and a good thing to keep in mind. But the Dreamspeakers don't, and shouldn't, have an inside track on just what the Avatar <i>is</i>; nobody should. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420739#post1420739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should have gotten to this earlier in my reply:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420592#post1420592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we assign a value in gigabytes</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant data like gigs, not Data Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; that's how I understood it. But it was a convenient point for me to address the fact that data is in the domain of Correspondence. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420739#post1420739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some things about the game that I find arbitrary. Besides Mind, Correspondence is one of the most powerful Spheres. Faced with a difficult situation? - Teleport to England (preferably the countryside). A little paradox to escape with your life. Then, adding the ability to alter computer data from a distance, you can shut down a power station from a distance, where a Forces Mage would have to get into line of sight and attack the building's exposed parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes is powerful <i>where data is concerned</i>; so its power is constrained. That said, I've explored a slightly different configuration of the Spheres that separates the location-like aspects of Correspondence from the data-relevant aspects, effectively splitting it into separate Space and Data Spheres. It's still something of a work in progress, though. See <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded\">Fields for the Technocracy</a> for more details. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420739#post1420739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find alternatives to materialism interesting. This interview had me up late. Couldn't stop listening.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Az18Onc0e58&amp;ab_channel=metaRising\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Az18...nel=metaRising</a></div> </div> </div> </div> My introduction to the notion came from <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books/about/Elemental_Mind.html?id=8cLWAAAAMAAJ&amp;source=kp_book_description\" target=\"_blank\">Elemental Mind</a>, by Nick Herbert. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420739#post1420739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose telling new players their character is special for having an avatar, you have to make it this elusive thing that can't be nailed down. I have not yet given Book Of The Fallen a complete read... There, said don't get me started on the Caul and look at me go.</div> </div> </div> </div> Again, my understanding is that <i>every</i> human has an Avatar; but only mages have <i>Awakened</i> Avatars. But yes, part of the point is that the Avatar is largely not subject to Magick: Gilgul requires Mastery of Spirit, and doing things too the Avatar <i>other than</i> ripping it to pieces is something that requires something more. In the MRev era, and specifically in <b>Ascension</b>, there was something about psychopomps that were responsible for guiding Avatars to their hosts, and a ritual that allowed a mage to fuse with a psychopomps to gain some ability to influence Avatar-related phenomena such as the Avatar Storm. This is something that hasn't shown up other than that one place (though some of the earlier MRev books foreshadowed it), so it's something you can choose to ignore of you want; but there <i>is</i> precedent for Avatars being mostly outside the scope of what Magick can affect. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107618-trinary-computers-how-create?p=1420739#post1420739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. Is there a TV-land?</div> </div> </div> </div> The Digital Web intersects with the Internet, too, and with TV, radio, and the like; those things all exist on the \u201cskin\u201d of the Hypersphere, and so the Digital Web intersects with them. So yes, there is a TV-land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-28-2020, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}